Static files served from the web root.

Karo's icons, web manifest, robots.txt and sitemap are generated by the App
Router instead (`src/app/icon.svg`, `manifest.ts`, `robots.ts`, `sitemap.ts`),
so this directory is empty today.

It is kept in version control because the `runner` stage of the Dockerfile
copies it unconditionally, and Docker's `COPY` fails the build when its source
is missing. Keeping the directory means adding a genuinely static asset later is
a drop-in, with no deployment change and no broken image.
